```rust
struct PrefixErrFuture<F> {
    prefix: &'static str,
    inner: F,
}

impl<F> PrefixErrFuture<F> {
    fn new(prefix: &'static str, inner: F) -> Self {
        Self { prefix, inner }
    }
}

impl<F, T, E> Future for PrefixErrFuture<F>
where
    F: Future<Output = Result<T, E>>,
    E: std::fmt::Display,
{
    type Output = Option<T>;

    fn poll(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Self::Output> {
        let prefix = self.prefix;
        let inner = unsafe { Pin::new_unchecked(&mut self.get_unchecked_mut().inner) };
        match inner.poll(cx) {
            Poll::Ready(output) => Poll::Ready(match output {
                Ok(value) => Some(value),
                Err(error) => {
                    log::error!("{prefix}: {error}");
                    None
                }
            }),
            Poll::Pending => Poll::Pending,
        }
    }
}
```

Note: named struct instead of tuple to show field access `self.prefix` — mirrors source semantics (self.1). Using struct with fields makes projection clearer. prefix read via Deref before get_unchecked_mut — same as source reading self.1/self.2. 

Important caveat to state: this struct must not implement Drop; never move `inner` out; that's the soundness contract (same as gpui_util's).

